Fair value is the sum of the three dice means: 5.75 + 5 + 5.25 = 16.0. The settlement standard deviation is about 6.6, roughly the same as the noise traders' spread.

I weighed noise-trader profit against losses to informed traders. Expected profit per side is highest at a half-spread of about 0.9 standard deviations, which is about 6. So I quote 10 / 22, centred on 16.

