Before any cards are revealed, the expected sum of three cards is 3 × 7 = 21. The standard deviation of the sum is about 6.35, because the cards are drawn without replacement.

I compared expected profit per side for different half-spreads around 21. I weighed what I earn from noise traders (spread 4.8) against what I lose to the informed trader, who knows the exact sum. Profit is roughly flat between half-spreads of 4 and 5, so I'll use about 4.5.

