Fair value is about 23.4, since the 10 cards average 7.8 and 3 are dealt. The quote 1 no-trade barely moves it because that quote was symmetric. The 3-card sum has a standard deviation of about 7.2, and noise traders scatter with a standard deviation of 5.4.

On a normal approximation, profit from noise traders roughly offsets losses to informed traders across most widths. The edge is thin and is best around a half-spread of 8 to 8.5. I'll keep the spread roughly as wide as last time and centred on 23.4.

