Card 1 was a 12, so 12 cards remain. Their values sum to 41, which is about 3.42 per card. The expected sum of the two unrevealed cards is about 6.83, so fair value is about 18.8. The trading history barely changes this.

The two unrevealed cards together have a standard deviation of about 4.2. Noise traders' valuations are wide (standard deviation 8.9), so I can quote a fairly wide spread and still trade with them. I set the half-spread at roughly 3.7 around fair. I am short 1, so I shift the quotes up slightly to make buying a little more likely than selling.

